0..41 Comment "/// Actions whose arguments reduce alike."
42..45 Comment "///"
46..120 Comment "/// An action on a path that is itself an action is one path, wherever the"
121..196 Comment "/// source writes the inner action. `whiskerAlong` unfolds to the action of"
197..271 Comment "/// composing with `g`. So a call of it and the action written out are one"
272..346 Comment "/// argument, beneath another action or another whisker. The nested action"
347..420 Comment "/// written in one definition is the same path as the outer action on the"
421..435 Comment "/// inner one."
436..439 Comment "///"
440..513 Comment "/// Each outer action unfolds to a transport whose motive reads the inner"
514..591 Comment "/// path. That path is the endpoint a transport along `fa` returns, held once"
592..663 Comment "/// per writing. The engine sets the two endpoints aside and reads each"
664..740 Comment "/// through to its transport. It emits the motives as one shared comparison,"
741..787 Comment "/// which the kernel replays on its own terms."
788..791 Comment "///"
792..867 Comment "/// - see: #3976 — the code walk pairs a lambda\'s captures laid out apart"
868..941 Comment "/// - see: #4005 — the checker refused two such endpoints inside a code"
943..972 Comment "/// The action of `F` on `p`."
